        "original_id": "7ccc9fe3-6947-5aa1-b318-8c211a941d36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Arundel Castle, Sussex, Norfolk\n- Events: English Civil War\n- People/Roles: Duke of Norfolk, Parliamentarians, Royalists\n- Topics: England's government\n\nFacts:\n- The English Civil War lasted from 1642 to 1651 and was a series of armed conflicts and political machinations between Parliamentarians (\"Roundheads\") and Royalists (\"Cavaliers\") over the manner of England's government.\n- Arundel Castle was damaged during the English Civil War.\n- Arundel Castle was restored in the 18th and 19th centuries.\n- Arundel Castle in Sussex is the seat of the Duke of Norfolk.\n- The title Duke of Norfolk refers to the county of Norfolk, although the seat is Arundel Castle in Sussex.",
